# Agent notes for {{ distribution }}

{{ description }}

Read [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) first; it is written for humans and is
accurate. This file records what is easy to get wrong.

## Commands

Use the tasks, not the underlying tools — they carry the flags CI uses:

```bash
mise run install    # the environment
mise run ci         # format:check, lint, typecheck, cover{% if docs %}, docs:build{% endif %}
mise run test -k X  # a subset
```
{% if is_pdm %}
The task host is PDM. `mise run <task>` delegates to `pdm run <task>`; the
canonical definitions are `[tool.pdm.scripts]` in `pyproject.toml`.
{% else %}
The task host is mise. The canonical definitions are `[tasks.*]` in
`mise.toml`; `pyproject.toml` has no scripts table and should not grow one.
{% endif %}
Always `mise run <task>`, never bare `mise <task>`: a mise builtin subcommand
of the same name wins silently and says nothing about the task it shadowed.

## Constraints that are not obvious

- **Python {{ python_min }} is the floor.** `ty` checks against it, and the CI
  matrix runs the tests on it. A construct newer than {{ python_min }} is an
  error even though the development interpreter is {{ python_default }}.
- **The supported range is derived, not written down.** `requires-python`, the
  trove classifiers, the ruff `target-version`, the ty environment and the CI
  matrix all come from one answer in the template. Do not edit one of them to
  fix a mismatch — they cannot mismatch, so a mismatch means the file is stale
  and the fix is `git tpl merge`.
- **The version.**{% if is_pdm %} It is the Git tag. `pyproject.toml` declares
  `dynamic = ["version"]` and pdm-backend reads the tag at build time. There is
  no version string to edit, and adding one would be a second, divergent
  source of truth.{% else %} It is `project.version` in `pyproject.toml`, and
  `cz bump` owns it. Do not edit it by hand; if you do, `uv.lock` is
  immediately stale and the `uv-lock-check` hook fails the commit.{% endif %}
- **Commit subjects are Conventional Commits**, validated on `commit-msg` and
  used verbatim as changelog entries.
- **`# --- project-specific ---` markers** separate template-owned lines from
  the project's own. Add below the marker. Editing above it means the next
  `git tpl merge` conflicts.

## Where things live

```
src/{{ package }}/       the package
tests/                   pytest, mirroring src/
{% if docs %}docs/                    the documentation site (zensical.toml drives the nav)
{% endif %}.github/workflows/       CI and release
mise.toml                toolchain{% if not is_pdm %} and tasks{% endif %}
prek.toml                the hooks — almost all `local`, running the installed tools
```

## Do not

- Add a `.pre-commit-config.yaml`. The hooks live in `prek.toml`; two config
  formats for one runner means one of them is stale.
- Add mypy, black, isort or flake8. ruff and ty cover all four, and running two
  linters means arbitrating between them forever.
- Pin a tool version in `prek.toml` that is already floored in
  `[dependency-groups]`. The two drift, and the hook then disagrees with CI.
- Commit `.venv`{% if is_pdm %}, `src/{{ package }}/VERSION`{% endif %} or
  `coverage.xml`.
